REMINISCENCE — MISSING IMPLEMENTATION PLAN
===============================================

Purpose
-------
Track implementation that remains missing or partial in the current Reminiscene
repository. Update this file whenever a subsystem moves from MISSING to PARTIAL
or PARTIAL to DONE.

STATUS
------
DONE       = implemented and validated
PARTIAL    = foundation exists; production path incomplete
MISSING    = implementation not yet present
BLOCKED    = depends on hardware, model artifact, or external integration

P0 — RELEASE-BLOCKING
=====================

1. Configuration consolidation — PARTIAL
   Files: reminiscence/app/config/*, .env.example, docs/*
   - Centralize environment-driven settings.
   - Make CLI, engine, workers, storage and model manager consume the same paths.
   - Document all supported variables.
   Done when a clean machine starts using only documented configuration.

2. Production multimodal ingestion — PARTIAL
   Files: reminiscence/ingestion/*
   - Complete PDF/DOCX/PPTX extraction edge cases.
   - Complete audio decoding and ASR event generation.
   - Complete image OCR/event generation.
   - Connect video keyframes, ASR and OCR.
   - Enforce file type, size and resource limits.
   Done when every declared format either ingests successfully or returns a
   deterministic unsupported/error state and ingestion is idempotent.

3. Production ASR — PARTIAL
   Files: reminiscence/ai/asr/asr.py, ingestion/audio/*, ai/model_manager.py
   - Finish Whisper/ONNX inference.
   - Preserve segment timestamps/language.
   - Record actual execution provider.
   - Provide explicit CPU fallback.
   Done when real local audio produces searchable timestamped MemoryEvents.

4. Production OCR/Vision — PARTIAL
   Files: reminiscence/ai/vision/*, ingestion/images/*
   - Finish ONNX OCR inference.
   - Map regions into searchable events.
   - Preserve confidence/provenance.
   - Add optional visual understanding.
   Done when image text is searchable with source/confidence metadata.

5. Local LLM + EvidencePack — MISSING/PARTIAL
   Files: reminiscence/ai/llm/*, reminiscence/evidence/*
   - Add local LLM runtime adapter.
   - Define EvidencePack as grounded context contract.
   - Generate only from resolved evidence.
   - Attach source/event references to claims.
   Done when answers remain grounded and expose citations/references.

6. Memory Graph service — PARTIAL
   Files: storage/database.py, memory/events.py, new reminiscence/graph/*
   - Entity extraction for people and places.
   - Entity resolution/normalization.
   - Graph traversal and multi-hop retrieval.
   - Timeline/entity graph service.
   Done when people/places link to memories and graph retrieval contributes evidence.

7. Retrieval-quality evaluation — MISSING
   Files: retrieval/*, benchmarks/*, new benchmark datasets
   - Build deterministic query/relevance cases.
   - Measure recall@k, precision@k, MRR/nDCG where applicable.
   - Compare lexical, vector, temporal, graph and hybrid retrieval.
   Done when offline runs are reproducible and record configuration.

P1 — CORE PRODUCT
=================

8. PySide6 desktop UI — MISSING
   Files: reminiscence/app/ui/*
   - Main window, import, search, ask, timeline, sources, media viewer,
     evidence panel, jobs and settings.
   - Keep long-running work off the UI thread.
   Done when UI and CLI share the same service/engine layer.

9. Incremental indexing — PARTIAL
   Files: ingestion/pipeline.py, storage/*, workers/queue.py
   - Persist fingerprints.
   - Detect unchanged and moved files.
   - Re-index only changed extraction/embedding versions.
   Done when repeated ingestion creates no duplicates and model-version changes
   invalidate only dependent work.

10. Backup/export — MISSING
    Files: storage/media_store.py, new storage/backup.py, storage/export.py
    - Portable memory/metadata/media export.
    - Backup manifest and restore validation.
    Done when export is portable and corruption/missing media is detectable.

11. Secure deletion — MISSING
    Files: storage/*, app/services/engine.py
    - Remove source, dependent events, media, vector entries and graph links.
    Done when deleted content is absent from lexical, vector, graph and evidence
    retrieval paths.

12. Security hardening — PARTIAL
    Files: .github/workflows/security.yml, ingestion/*, ai/model_manager.py
    - Make security gates blocking.
    - Add resource-exhaustion limits.
    - Harden malicious/invalid file handling.
    - Isolate temporary files and redact sensitive logs.
    - Strengthen model provenance/signature policy.
    Done when required security checks fail the build on failure.

13. CI quality gates — PARTIAL
    Files: .github/workflows/ci.yml, pyproject.toml
    - Make mypy blocking after cleanup.
    - Add clean-install/package smoke tests.
    - Verify wheel/sdist contents.
    Done when CI passes without ignored required failures.

P2 — ADVANCED
=============

14. Video semantic understanding — MISSING
    - Scene segmentation.
    - Semantic video embeddings.
    - Multimodal alignment of ASR/OCR/keyframes.
    Done when queries can retrieve relevant video timestamps.

15. People/face pipeline — MISSING
    - Explicit opt-in face embeddings.
    - Identity assignment and manual correction.
    - Revocation/deletion path.
    Done when biometric processing is disabled by default and fully removable.

16. Place extraction/geographic normalization — PARTIAL
    - Normalize EXIF/GPS and textual place mentions.
    - Preserve source/confidence.
    - Never make external geocoding a hidden dependency.

17. Snapdragon/QNN validation — BLOCKED until target hardware
    - Validate actual QNN/NPU execution.
    - Record provider/model/quantization.
    - Compare CPU/NPU latency and power where observable.
    Done when NPU claims are backed by actual provider telemetry.

18. Observability — PARTIAL
    - Structured inference/job/retrieval telemetry.
    - No raw personal content in normal logs.
    Done when failures and performance regressions are diagnosable safely.

19. Release engineering — PARTIAL
    - Version policy, release workflow, clean platform installation and artifact
      validation.
    Done when a clean install from the built artifact succeeds.

IMPLEMENTATION ORDER
====================
A. Stabilize: configuration -> hygiene -> CI/security -> ingestion limits
B. Engine: ASR -> OCR -> incremental indexing -> retrieval evaluation
C. Intelligence: graph -> EvidencePack/local LLM -> backup/export -> deletion
D. Product: PySide6 UI -> media/evidence viewer -> settings/jobs
E. Advanced: video -> people/places -> Snapdragon/QNN -> observability/release

DEFINITION OF DONE
==================
Every completed item must have:
- implementation integrated into the main architecture
- automated normal/failure-path tests
- provenance and source metadata
- privacy/offline-by-default compliance
- measured runtime/provider claims
- matching documentation
- passing required CI/security gates

MVP NON-GOALS
=============
- distributed/cloud workers
- mandatory cloud AI
- silent online model downloads
- biometric processing by default
- unconstrained generation without grounded retrieval
